  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A thin convex lens is placed just above an empty vessel of depth $80 \\mathrm{~cm}$. The image of a coin kept at the bottom of the vessel is thus formed $20 \\mathrm{~cm}$ above the lens. If now water is poured in the vessel up to a height of $64 \\mathrm{~cm}$, what will be the approximate new position of the image. Assume that refractive index of water is $4 / 3$.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "KSFzl",
      "text": "$21.33 \\mathrm{~cm}$ above the lens",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "iMM2P",
      "text": "$6.67 \\mathrm{~cm}$ below the lens",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Lu0eY",
      "text": "$33.67 \\mathrm{~cm}$ above the lens",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "BZPVH",
      "text": "$24 \\mathrm{~cm}$ above the lens",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint: \r\n$\\mathrm{u}=-80 \\mathrm{~cm} \\quad \\mathrm{v}=+20 \\mathrm{~cm}$\r\n$\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{f}}=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{v}}-\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{u}}=\\frac{1}{20}+\\frac{1}{80}=\\frac{5}{80}$\r\n$f=16 \\mathrm{~cm}$\r\n$\\mathrm{u}^{\\prime}=16+\\frac{64 \\times 3}{4}=64 \\mathrm{~cm}$\r\n$\\frac{1}{16}=\\frac{1}{v}+\\frac{1}{64} \\quad \\therefore \\frac{1}{v}=\\frac{1}{16}-\\frac{1}{64}=\\frac{3}{64}$\r\n$v=21.33$ above the lens\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/wWvSiRxqb37vSqr-EwBryKodqsZrEEsQlra4EwdCv1w.original.fullsize.png\">",
